Charlie had 10 stickers. He picked up 21 more from a store in the mall and got 23 for his birthday. Then he gave 9 to his sister and used 28 to deck out a greeting card. How many stickers does Charlie have left?,Charlie had 10 stickers. He bought 21 stickers from a store in the mall and got 23 stickers for his birthday. Then Charlie gave 9 of the stickers to his sister and used 28 to decorate a greeting card. How many stickers does Charlie have left?,17,17,17,17,"Charlie started with 10 stickers. After picking up 21 more, he had 10 + 21 = 31. Adding the 23 from his birthday brought him to 31 + 23 = 54. He then gave away 9 stickers, leaving 54 - 9 = 45. Finally, using 28 stickers for the card resulted in 45 - 28 = 17 stickers remaining.

