But she pauses for half an hour. Half an hour is 30 minutes. So I need to subtract that break time from the total time. So 180 minutes minus 30 minutes equals 150 minutes of actual working time.

Now, she earns $5 every 10 minutes. To find out how many 10-minute intervals are in 150 minutes, I divide 150 by 10. Let me do that calculation: 150 ÷ 10 = 15. So there are 15 intervals of 10 minutes each.

