Next, she tripled the number of slices she currently has because she was getting hungrier. Hmm, tripling means multiplying by 3. So she had 5 slices, then triples them. So 5 multiplied by 3. 5 * 3 is 15. Now she has 15 slices.

Then she ate 2 slices. So we subtract 2 from the current total. 15 minus 2 is 13. So after eating, there are 13 slices left.

