"Andrew whipped up 200 mini cinnamon rolls and 300 mini blueberry muffins. A regular cinnamon roll packs 600 calories and a regular blueberry muffin has 450 calories. If a mini one has just 1/3rd the calories of the normal ones, how many calories are in all the pastries he made?","Andrew bakes 200 mini cinnamon rolls and 300 mini blueberry muffins. A normal cinnamon roll has 600 calories and a normal blueberry muffin has 450 calories. If a mini pastry has 1/3rd of the calories of a normal version, how many calories do the pastries he baked have?",85000,85000,850,850,"Andrew made 200 mini cinnamon rolls and 300 mini blueberry muffins. Each mini cinnamon roll has 1/3 of 600 calories, which is 200 calories. Each mini blueberry muffin has 1/3 of 450 calories, which is 150 calories. 

Calculating the total calories:
- Cinnamon rolls: 200 pastries × 200 calories = 40,000 calories
- Blueberry muffins: 300 pastries × 150 calories = 45,000 calories

Adding both totals: 40,000 + 45,000 = 85,000 calories.

#### 85000","Okay, let's see. Andrew made these mini pastries, right? So the problem says he made 200 mini cinnamon rolls and 300 mini blueberry muffins. The question is about figuring out the total calories in all of them. Let me break this down step by step.

