Adding those two together: 40,000 + 45,000. 40k + 40k is 80k, then plus 5k makes 85k. So 85,000 total calories.

Hmm, did I miss anything? Let me check again. The problem says calories in all the pastries. So cinnamon rolls and muffins combined. Yep. Mini versions are 1/3 of regular calories. So original cinnamon is 600, divided by 3 gives 200. Original muffin is 450, divided by 3 gives 150. That's right. So yes, the calculation seems correct.
