","The hospital starts with 1/5 of 1000 beds occupied, which is 200 beds. Initially, there are 800 unoccupied beds (1000 - 200). Over 14 days, 50 new patients are admitted each day, totaling 700 additional patients (50 × 14). Total occupied beds after 2 weeks become 200 + 700 = 900. Subtracting this from the total capacity gives 1000 - 900 = 100 unoccupied beds.
