","First, determine the number of female porcupines in the initial population. Since 3/5 of the 50 porcupines are females:
\[
\frac{3}{5} \times 50 = 30 \text{ female porcupines}
\]
Each female produces 4 babies every month. The number of babies produced each month by all females is:
\[
30 \times 4 = 120 \text{ babies per month}
