"My kitchen floor is 200 SqFt big. I'm looking to put in new square tiles that are $12 a pop, and each tile is 1ft on each side. How much is it gonna cost me to redo the floor?","My kitchen floor has a total area of 200 SqFt. I want to install new square floor tiles that cost $12 each, and each tile side is 1ft in length. How much will it cost me to renovate my kitchen floor?",2400,2400,240,240,"The kitchen floor is 200 square feet. Each tile covers 1 square foot, so 200 tiles are needed. Each tile costs $12, so the total cost is 200 tiles × $12/tile = $2400. #### 2400","Okay, let's see. The problem is about calculating the cost to redo a kitchen floor with new tiles. The kitchen is 200 square feet. Each tile is 1 foot on each side, so each tile covers 1 square foot. Each tile costs $12. So I need to figure out how many tiles are needed and then multiply by the cost per tile to get the total cost.

